  "Compose@@email": "",
  "Size sets scale, ink sets hierarchy. Between them they cover nearly every text decision in the app — reach for a different weight only when both are already right.": "",
  "Sizes": "",
  "`text-sm` is the default for UI chrome; `text-base` is for reading surfaces such as documents and messages.": "",
  "Hierarchy": "",
  "Establish rank with ink before reaching for size or weight. Two ink steps read as a clear hierarchy at the same size.": "",
  "Size × ink": "",
  "Every combination at a glance. Check the lower-contrast inks stay legible when you change a theme with the toolbar above.": "",
  "depth={depth}": "",
  "depth=": "",
  "Hello!": "",
  "depth 0": "",
  "depth 1": "",
  "depth 2": "",
  "depth 3": "",
  "Layer offset=": "",
  "Outline": "",
  "Depth, not a chosen color, is how backgrounds are set. A container declares its depth and everything inside reads `bg-surface` and `bg-inset` relative to it — so the same component looks right wherever it is nested.": "",
  "The depth scale": "",
  "Depth 0 sits furthest back and 4 closest to the viewer. `Panel` and `Surface` take a `depth` prop; `Layer` marks a subtree without rendering a box.": "",
  "Nesting": "",
  "Each level steps forward, which is what makes nested containers legible without borders doing all the work.": "",
  "Layer-relative tokens": "",
  "`bg-inset` sits one step back and `bg-surface` is the layer itself. To move content forward, wrap it in `Layer offset={1}` and continue using `bg-surface`.": "",
  "Controls across depths": "",
  "Check any new component here. Contrast that only works at one depth is the most common design-system regression in the app.": "",
  "Every color in the app comes from a semantic token, never a raw Tailwind color. Themes redefine the tokens; components never change.": "",
  "Surfaces": "",
  "The background ramp. Components read these through the layer system rather than naming a step directly — see Surfaces & Depth.": "",
  "Text colors, from primary down to placeholder. `ink-extra-muted` is a deprecated alias for `ink-subtle`; use `ink-subtle` in new code.": "",
  "Semantic": "",
  "Meaning-carrying colors. Reach for these before the raw palette so intent survives a theme change.": "",
  "Named hues for content that needs a color of its own — labels, calendars, avatars. Not for conveying state.": "",
