  "Workspace URL": "",
  "Enter the full workspace URL.": "",
  "An accessible, slot-based text input and textarea. Kobalte connects labels, descriptions, and errors while the controls use the app’s layer-aware tokens.": "",
  "The root owns value state and automatically connects the label and description to the input.": "",
  "Textarea": "",
  "`TextField.TextArea` shares the same root API. `autoResize` lets Kobalte grow it with its content.": "",
  "Disabled and invalid": "",
  "Root state flows to every slot. Invalid controls receive `aria-invalid`, and the error message is included in `aria-describedby`.": "",
  "design": "",
  "A small, non-interactive label for status, counts, and tags. Shares Button’s size scale so a badge and a button of the same size sit on the same line cleanly.": "",
  "`ghost` when the surrounding container already provides separation, `outline` when the badge needs its own edge.": "",
  "Matches the Button `sm` / `md` / `lg` control sizes.": "",
  "Composed content": "",
  "Badges take arbitrary children — a color dot for a tag, a status glyph, a caret when the badge is the visible half of a menu trigger.": "",
  "Full access, including billing": "",
  "Manage members and settings": "",
  "Create and edit content": "",
  "Guest": "",
  "View shared items only": "",
  "A Kobalte select, styled for the app. It is slot-based: you supply the trigger and the item renderer, while `Select.Content` handles portalling, popper sizing, menu chrome, and its own layer depth.": "",
  "`optionValue` and `optionTextValue` tell the collection which fields identify and label each option. `Select.Value` receives the selected option, so the trigger renders whatever you want.": "",
  "Rich items": "",
  "`itemComponent` renders arbitrary content. Keep `Select.ItemLabel` around the primary text so typeahead and the accessible name still work.": "",
  "A disabled select keeps its value visible but will not open.": "",
  "Panel.Header": "",
  "Toolbar": "",
  "Action": "",
  "Panel.Body takes the remaining height and is the only slot that shrinks.": "",
  "Scrolling body": "",
  "Row {row}": "",
  "active": "",
  "A depth-aware container with fixed header, toolbar, and footer slots around a body that absorbs the remaining height. The layout is a CSS grid, so the body scrolls without the chrome moving.": "",
  "Slots": "",
  "Every slot is optional and renders nothing when empty, so a body-only Panel has no stray borders.": "",
  "`Panel.Body scroll` wraps the content in `Scroll`, keeping the header and footer pinned. Give the Panel a bounded height for this to take effect.": "",
  "Active state": "",
  "`active` draws the focus ring used for the panel holding keyboard focus in a split layout.": "",
  "Read receipts": "",
  "Let others see when you read a message.": "",
  "Typing indicators": "",
  "Show when you are composing.": "",
  "An on/off switch for a setting that applies immediately. If the change needs a save step, use a Checkbox instead.": "",
  "Controlled via `checked` and `onChange`, or uncontrolled via `defaultChecked`. The whole component — including the gap between control and label — is one hit target.": "",
  "`sm` is the default toolbar size; `md` is for settings rows; `xs` is for dense inline chrome.": "",
  "Settings row": "",
  "The standard settings pattern: label and description on the left, switch on the right.": "",
